  "findings": [
    "Fixed-N anomalous average vanishes; pairing correlations and pair transfer can remain finite. Pairing fluctuations are not Var(N).",
    "PNC pair-Hamiltonian off-diagonal matrix elements, one-body Jx interference, and two-body pair coherence must be kept distinct.",
    "105Cd pairing delays/smooths the neutron crossing but makes proton-hole closure more obvious; 104Pd has faster low-frequency closure and slower high-frequency closure. No universal slowing law.",
    "PNC exactness is confined to the selected Hamiltonian and truncated fixed-N space. Real symmetry-sector crossings remain possible.",
    "LN is an approximate number-projection correction distinct from uncorrected BCS; weak-pairing failure is model dependent; PHFB provides an alternative.",
    "Fixed-deformation PNC does not reproduce all high-frequency B(E2) decrease in 106Cd or 104Pd; fitted deformation is not independent experimental evidence."
  ],
  "finite_model_controls": [
    "Same-H exact N=2 versus BCS: at G=.8 MeV, epsilon=.4 MeV, BCS gap=0 but exact pair-transfer coherence=1/sqrt(2).",
    "Effective constant-W mixing broadens a crossing at omega=.4 without moving its center; at W=0 the crossing eigenstate is not unique.",
    "Exact-N two-sector cranking gives a genuine crossing at omega=.89442719 MeV/hbar for epsilon=.2, G=.8."
  ],
